WHAT Ms-PL COVERS HERE, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
============================================

This directory is not licensed uniformly, and saying otherwise would be a false
statement about other people's code.  A device port is a small amount of new work
threaded through a large amount of existing work, and the existing work keeps its
own terms.

Ms-PL, the licence below:

    build-in-vm.sh              the incremental bring-up builder
    generate_dts.py             the DTS generator
    create_boot_image.py        the MT6592 Android boot.img writer
    fetch_freedoom.py           the optional Freedoom fetcher
    sync-mvii-board.sh          the by-hand MVII driver refresh
    es/patch-gles20.py          the EmulationStation CMake patch generator
    tools/j36-eglprobe.c        the EGL/GBM/DRM scanout probe
    tools/mfgpower.c            the MFG power-domain bring-up probe
    README.md, this file        the documentation

    Each of those carries an `SPDX-License-Identifier: MS-PL' header, with one
    deliberate exception: es/patch-gles20.py has none, because build-in-vm.sh
    stamps the EmulationStation build with a SHA-256 of that file, so editing it at
    all -- even to add a comment -- discards a finished ES build and rebuilds it
    from scratch.  It is Ms-PL by this listing instead.

GPL-2.0-only, and deliberately NOT relicensed:

    linux/j36_mt6592_input.c    keypad and GPIO key adapter
    linux/j36_mt6592_audio.c    MT6592 AFE ASoC card
    linux/j36_jd9365_panel.c    the JD9365 panel that adopts LK's state
    linux/0001-mtk-sd-mt6592.patch
    linux/0002-drm-mediatek-mt6592.patch

    These are Linux kernel modules and Linux kernel patches.  They carry
    `SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only' and `MODULE_LICENSE("GPL v2")', they
    are derivative of and link against GPL-2.0-only kernel internals, and the two
    patches are diffs against GPL-2.0-only files.  Ms-PL is not GPL-compatible --
    its section 3(D) imposes a condition GPLv2 section 6 forbids adding -- so
    relicensing them is not something this project is free to do, and it does not
    try.  Send changes to them upstream; they are GPL either way.

EmulationStation's own terms:

    es/Renderer_GLES20.cpp      a renderer for EmulationStation-fcamod, written to
                                drop into that project's es-core/src/renderers/
                                directory alongside its two existing renderers.
                                It is a derivative of that tree and follows its
                                licence, not this one.

Vendor material, redistributed unmodified for provenance:

    mvii-board/                 five verbatim MediaTek/MVII board headers and
                                driver sources, listed with a SHA-256 each in
                                mvii-board/PROVENANCE.txt.  They are inputs the
                                DTS generator parses, not MixOS work, and they
                                carry whatever terms their authors set.

Nothing in this file changes the licence of anything a build downloads or stages:
the Linux kernel, Mesa, SDL, EmulationStation, busybox, the Debian rootfs and the
Freedoom IWAD are each obtained under their own terms and are not covered here.
A card built by `build-in-vm.sh' is an aggregate of many licences; Ms-PL applies
to the MixOS scripts and probes that assembled it.


