ATTRIBUTION
===========

MixOS is a divergent fork of dArkOS, which is itself a Debian-based continuation
of ArkOS.  Neither project asked for this port, neither endorses it, and neither
is responsible for it.  Full attribution and thanks are in ../../LICENSES.md and
../../README.md at the top of this repository; the short form is:

  * Debian -- the operating system underneath all of it.  The rootfs a MixOS card
    boots is Debian, built with Debian's own tools, and every package outside
    this directory that is not the kernel came from Debian.  https://www.debian.org
  * ArkOS, by christianhaitian -- the original handheld distribution and the
    source of the layout, the tools menu and the EmulationStation integration.
  * dArkOS -- the Debian rebuild of ArkOS this repository was forked from, and
    the origin of everything outside device/j36-ultra/ and device/r36-ultra/.
  * MediaTek -- the MT6592 register-level documentation and the vendor driver
    sources this port reads, via the MVII tree in mvii-board/.
  * The Linux kernel, Mesa (lima and kmsro), SDL, EmulationStation, busybox,
    doomgeneric and Freedoom, without any of which there would be no port.
